WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.395
A secure ASP.

2
00:00:01.395 --> 00:00:05.303
NET Core baseline starts with the application lifecycle.

3
00:00:05.303 --> 00:00:11.164
Security belongs in architecture, coding, configuration, deployment, and operations.

4
00:00:11.164 --> 00:00:22.257
The request pipeline should make transport, routing, errors, authentication, authorization, and endpoints work together in a way the team can explain and test.

5
00:00:22.257 --> 00:00:25.886
Authenticate explicitly and authorize on the server.

6
00:00:25.886 --> 00:00:28.467
Authentication identifies the caller.

7
00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:31.677
Authorization decides what that caller may do.

8
00:00:31.677 --> 00:00:41.305
Access rules should protect MVC actions, Razor Pages, controllers, APIs, Minimal APIs, operational endpoints, and administrative surfaces.

9
00:00:41.305 --> 00:00:46.189
User interface hints are not a substitute for server-side enforcement.

10
00:00:46.189 --> 00:00:47.864
Protect state carefully.

11
00:00:47.864 --> 00:00:59.795
Cookies can carry security-sensitive state, antiforgery protections help with state-changing browser requests, CORS is not identity, and session state should be minimized.

12
00:00:59.795 --> 00:01:11.796
Configuration and secrets are also part of state: keep secrets out of source control, use appropriate secret storage, and plan Data Protection key persistence and rotation.

13
00:01:11.796 --> 00:01:13.540
Handle data deliberately.

14
00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:31.193
Validate input on the server, shape request DTOs carefully, avoid over-posting, preserve Razor encoding defaults, avoid raw rendering of untrusted content, shape API responses, control error details, and handle files with limits and clear storage rules.

15
00:01:31.193 --> 00:01:35.100
Security is strongest when data boundaries are explicit.

16
00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:37.403
Finally, operate the application.

17
00:01:37.403 --> 00:01:42.915
Log meaningful security and operational events without exposing sensitive data.

18
00:01:42.915 --> 00:01:54.427
Monitor trends, review production configuration, keep dependencies current, plan secret rotation, prepare for incidents, and improve after real operational feedback.

19
00:01:54.427 --> 00:02:02.730
Security is not a one-time setting; it is an engineering habit that keeps the application understandable as it changes.
